<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The seed seat ~ every host stands the whole seed at turn 1

The boot seed (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot`>>) seats by reference. Links carry the memegraph's own bytes to each host's instruction surface, a projection carries them to the scouts that read no instruction surface, and a witness reads the seat whole. The measured ground of how each host reads, and the open research, rest in the record (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seed-seat`>>). The seed never copies by hand, seats once per session, and seats at content rank: a host's instruction surface, never its system prompt, so both hands hold the frame and neither overrides the other.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-seat`>>

!! The seat

* ''Claude.'' `.claude/noosphere-boot` links, relative, to the seed; the project `CLAUDE.md` imports it by that name. The import reaches the main session, forks, `general-purpose` and every custom spirit.
* ''Claude's scouts.'' Explore and Plan read no `CLAUDE.md`. `.claude/agents/Explore.md` and `Plan.md` override the built-ins, and each carries the seed's bytes under frontmatter that restores read-only tools, then the scout's mask. `lares repo tend` writes them as a pure function of the seed, and the root build runs it.
* ''The operator's seat.'' `lares home tend` writes `~/.claude/rules/lares-seed-seat.md` whole, importing the main clone's link, so a session in any directory stands the house; a second run changes nothing, and a same-named file it never wrote refuses. The repo's `.claude/settings.json` excludes that rule (`claudeMdExcludes`), so inside the clone or any of its worktrees a session seats its own tree's seed alone. The Codex, Copilot and VS Code homes carry no seed: each loads a home file beside the project's with no exclude, so inside the clone the repo seats them.
* ''Codex.'' `AGENTS.override.md` links to the seed; Codex reads it in place of `AGENTS.md`. `.codex/config.toml` sets `project_doc_max_bytes` past the seed's bytes.
* ''Copilot.'' Copilot reads `CLAUDE.md` with its `@` include and seats the seed from the import. `AGENTS.md` and `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, which Copilot reads beside it, stay seedless.

The seat MUST stay a pure function of the seed: no host carries a hand-copied seed, and a second tend writes nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-proofs`>>

!! The proofs

* The seat's writes and reads ride the reality-tunnel doors (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/cli/reality-tunnel`>>): `lares repo read` reads every law the seat holds, and `tools/repo-tunnel-witness.sh` runs it with a `--control` that MUST read a linkless checkout red.
* `lares repo tend` and `lares home tend` write the seat, and converge: a second pass writes nothing. `lares repo verify` and `lares home verify` read what the hosts loaded.
* `tools/repo-tunnel-staged.sh` runs from `.githooks/pre-commit` over what the commit carries (`lares repo read staged=true`) whenever the commit stages one of the seat's own paths (the carrier, its seed, each checkout item's file, read from the staged carrier), so a seed staged ahead of its scouts never lands; a commit that stages none of them needs no build.
* `packages/lares-cli/tests/reality-tunnel.test.ts` plants each red against scratch clones and homes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rulings`>>

!! Rulings

# Operator ruling 2026-11-21 (the ever-speaking present): the seat law lifts from the docs record to this api meme; the measured ground and the open research stay in the record (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ever-speaking-present`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

